            225  *       EVFX USES AN XOP CALL SINCE IT IS
            226  *       USED SO OFTEN AND RETURNS A 1 WORD,
            227  *       2'S COMPLEMENT INTEGER IN THE OPERAND
            228  *       OF THE EXOP.  EVFX DOES A FULL
            229  *       EVALUATION (R5 <> 0) AND RETURNS
            230  *       R0, R8, AND THE RESULT.
            231  *
            232  *       SINCE R0 IS ALTERED, EVFX R0 WOULD
            233  *       BE ILLEGAL.
            234  *
            235  * CALLING SEQUENCE:
            236  *
            237  *       XOP XX,11
            238  *
            239  *       IN  R8 = PBC
            240  *       OUT R0 = DLIM
            241  *           R8 = PBC UPDATED
            242  *         *R11 = #
            243  *
            244  * EXCEPTIONS AND CONDITIONS:
            245  *
            246  *       SAME AS EVSD WITH THE ADDITION OF
            247  *       A FIX ERROR POSSIBILITY.
            248  *
            249  *       R0,R8 CANNOT BE USED AS THE RETURNING
            250  *       FIELD.
            251  *
006C C80B   252  EVFX   MOV  R11,@RTSTOR       SAVE ADDRESS
006E 0000 
0070 06A0   253         BL   @EVALS            EVALUATE
0072 01D6'
0074 06A0   254         BL   @FIX              FIX RESULT
0076 0000 
0078 C320   255         MOV  @RTSTOR,R12       RESTORE RETURN ADDRESS
007A 006E'
007C C701   256         MOV  R1,*R12           RETURN #
007E 10F0   257         JMP  EVER2
ASM990 2.4.6     EVAL                       Sun Aug 10 23:07:35 2025 Page 0010
EVAL - CORTEX BASIC REV. 1.1

            259  *       EVAL IS A RECURSIVE STACK EXPRESSION EVALUATOR.
            260  *       R6 POINTS TO THE BOTTOM OF THE STACK WHERE
            261  *       OPERANDS AND OTHER DATA ARE STACKED
            262  *       WHILE R7 POINTS TO THE TOP OF THE STACK WHERE
            263  *       OPERATORS ARE STACKED.  BOTH ENDS OF THE STACK
            264  *       ARE MARKED WITH NULLS TO CHECK FOR PROPER
            265  *       EXPRESSION TERMINATION.  THE ROUTINE CONSISTS
            266  *       MAINLY OF A MULTIPLEXOR AND A PRECEDENCE ORIENTED
            267  *       PROCESSOR.
            268  *
            269  *       VARIABLES ARE STORED ON A STACK AS AN ADDRESS.
            270  *       CONSTANTS GO DIRECTLY ON THE STACK FOLLOWED BY
            271  *       A -1 TO INDICATE A CONSTANT VALUE.  IE:
            272  *
            273  *               * (PTR) * ----- /XXXX XXXX XXXX/
            274  *               * 4110  *
            275  *               * 0000  *
            276  *               * 0000  *
            277  *               *  -1   *
            278  *
            279  *       USER FUNCTIONS, SYSTEM FUNCTIONS, AND DIMENSIONED
            280  *       VARIABLES ALL RECURSE ON THE EVALUATOR TO
            281  *       OBTAIN THE ARGUMENTS.
            282  *
            283  *       THE LEFT BYTE OF R5 CONTROLS WHETHER A OPERATOR
            284  *       IS UNARY OR NOT.  WHEN NULL AND AN OPERATOR IS
            285  *       ENCOUNTERED, IT MUST BE UNARY!  UPON ENCOUNTERING
            286  *       A VARIABLE, THIS LEFT BYTE IS SET INDICATING
            287  *       THE NEXT OPERATOR WILL NOT BE UNARY.
            288  *
            289  *       THE RIGHT BYTE OF R5 CONTROLS HOW FAR THE
            290  *       EVALUATION IS TO GO.  IE, ONE ONLY WANTS THE
            291  *       FIRST VARIABLE FOR AN ASSIGNMENT STATEMENT OR
            292  *       ANYWHERE ONE WANTS TO STORE A VALUE.  THUS,
            293  *       WHEN THE RIGHT BYTE OF R5 IS ZERO, EVALUATION
            294  *       WILL TERMINATE AT THE FIRST OPERATOR.
            295  *
            296  *       WHEN A DELIMITER IS ENCOUNTED, THE RIGHT BYTE
            297  *       OF R5 IS SET TO ZERO THUS TERMINATING THE
            298  *       EVALUATION OF THE EXPRESSION.
            299  *
            300  *       THE LEAST SIGNIFICANT BIT OF THE OPERATOR
            301  *       ADDRESS IS USED TO INDICATE A UNARY OPERATION.
            302  *
            303  *       USER FUNCTIONS USE THE STACK QUITE EXTENSIVELY
            304  *       PUSHING FUNCTION ADDRESS, DUMMY ARGUMENTS, PLC,
            305  *       R5, AND A RETORE-STACK-POINTER (R4) FOR EACH
            306  *       LEVEL OF FUNCTIONS.
            307  *
            308  * CALLING SEQUENCE:
            309  *
            310  *       BL @EVALS       ;START EVALUATION
            311  *
            312  *       IN  R5  = EXPRESSION FLAG
            313  *
            314  *         (FALL THRU TO EVAL)
            315  *
            316  *       BL @EVAL        ;RECURSIVE EVALUATOR
            317  *
            318  *           R5  = EXPRESSION FLAG
ASM990 2.4.6     EVAL                       Sun Aug 10 23:07:35 2025 Page 0011
EVAL - CORTEX BASIC REV. 1.1

            319  *           R6  = BOTTOM OF STACK
            320  *           R7  = TOP OF STACK
            321  *           R8  = PLC
            322  *
            323  * EXCEPTIONS AND CONDITIONS:
            324  *
            325  *       IF R6 >= R7, THEN AN EXPRESSION TOO
            326  *          COMPLEX OCCURS.
ASM990 2.4.6     EVAL                       Sun Aug 10 23:07:35 2025 Page 0012
EVAL - CORTEX BASIC REV. 1.1

            328  *USER FUNCTION EVALUATION
